<!--
    Overlay on Playnite Default/Media.xaml.
    Icons are original drawings (art/glyphs.py, art/menu_icons.py), not the game's icon files: the props of the
    Vanilla interface (spellbook, hourglass, quill, banner, dice, compass) on a 24px grid, drawn by IconTemplate in
    the inherited foreground with a one pixel ink shadow, the way the client sets its text.

    Menu icons (main menu, game menu) are theme file paths: Playnite's MenuHelpers.GetIcon loads a string resource as
    an image through ThemeFile. Images/Menu holds the painted 48px versions. Sidebar Library and Statistics get their
    glyphs through CustomControls/SidebarItem.xaml.

    The client shows a question mark where an item has no icon; DefaultGameIcon and DefaultGameCover do the same for
    games without art.
-->
